-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Starquake
  Publisher   Bubble Bus Software, 1985
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Starquake (1985)(Bubble Bus).z80
  MD5         b94691b08d31386d3e5661d04e6c164f

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Note        No outline on the figures: the owner chose that for this mostly
              black game. The patch writes the whole alt ROM image (Sinclair's
              ROM plus its hooks), which fixed a crash on the define-keys
              screen. Known issues: the same keys can give different enemies
              from the unpatched game's, because the game seeds its random
              numbers from the frame counter and this build's start-up runs a
              little longer. Missing: no Enhanced colour set (rated moderate);
              pace not measured against the original; the cheats are unplayed
              by a person; not reached in testing: high-score name entry, the
              core assembly and the ending; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite energy
   3  No aliens
   4  Immunity

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

