-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by Jon Attree in JNext through the real loader,
              2026-11-04

  Replay      IDENTICAL on 9 recordings, 40884 frames (t1 2563 from the
              snapshot; b1-b3 8001/8001/8062 random play from an in-play state
              with infinite lives, energy and immunity poked; new from the
              snapshot: m1 4851 define keys, options 1-5, play with the new
              keys and pause, game over, define keys again from the post-game
              menu, play; m2-m4 3469/2457/2495 Kempston, cursor and Sinclair
              play with pause; m5 985 quit prompt N, define keys, quit Y to
              the goodbye screen and reset); three simulators in lockstep,
              hook fetches not counted, the patched machine's alt ROM built
              the way the Next's stub fills it, from NextZXOS ROM3: all memory
              but the screen against the original, and everything against the
              original with each frame's paint undone; sprite layer against an
              independent model every plot; hooks e_pl 28780, e_un 28780, e_rc
              218, e_cls 27, none never ran; 118383 figure plots, 17457337
              sprite pixels compared, 245 hides checked; 12 negatives each
              detected on a recording that exercises it, among them the
              30763c45 build's alt ROM (NextZXOS ROM3 code left round the
              hooks) and the old white outline; census over all 196 images: no
              outline pixel, no see-through hole, nothing at the canvas edge

  Emulator    JNext headless: the 30763c45 build crashes on the first key in
              define keys and hangs at any menu redraw (its alt ROM kept
              NextZXOS ROM3 code at 0x386E-, called by the IM 1 handler and
              the UDG print; four red figures and BLOB left as sprites),
              reproduced; this build defines keys from boot and after a game
              over with no stray sprites, the quit prompt, play with the new
              keys; plain, sprites and loading-screen .nex reach play; plain
              and sprites reach the same room, score and BLOB place at frame
              1650 with the same keys, enemies exactly as plain with the keys
              one frame earlier or later (the game reseeds its random numbers
              from FRAMES on entering a room, 0xA486, and this build's stub
              runs a little longer); hook cost about 49K T per frame counted
              at 3.5 MHz, run at 28 MHz; no white outline (owner, 2026-11-04)

  Coverage    about 130 screens by walking and falling, a Cheops pyramid
              screen, deaths; the menu, define keys twice (once from the menu
              after a game over), all five control options, pause, game over,
              the high-score table, the quit prompt both ways; 128 of the 196
              image slots drawn; not reached: high-score name entry, the core
              assembly, teleports by code (the code screen seen in JNext
              only), the ending; cheats from the archive's .pok for this
              release: lives, energy, immunity and no aliens shown in the
              simulator on the original code, unplayed by a person; no .256,
              no Enhanced set

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
